35,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The data reveals a shifting tide. While we have many eager minds for coding, the seasoned hands for phenotyping have vanished. We must ensure the project we choose has the actual human strength to survive.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Midori,,"It seems costs are shifting in unexpected ways. While some subsidies remain, others, like animal-unit rates and shipping, are rising. We must consider how these financial pressures might impact a researcher's actual capacity.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Wow, some good news and some bad! The animal facility is great, but the spectroscopy suite was down for eleven weeks! It's scary that only one engineer is covering three whole institutes. We need to be careful!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears the elements of nature are far less cooperative than our spreadsheets suggest. Between breeding colony failures and field site disasters, the risk of non-scientific delays is quite substantial. We must prioritize stability.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The data suggests a pattern. High-concept, mechanism-focused projects often stall, while those providing foundational resources continue to be useful long after the funding ends. We should value enduring utility over theoretical promise.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"It is a delicate balance, is it not? We seek the stars, yet we must keep our feet on the ground. A brilliant theory is but a ghost without the skilled hands to bring it to life.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Midori,,"I agree. It is so important that the researchers feel supported. If the costs of basic necessities are rising, it might put an unfair burden on the team's well-being and their focus.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"That's so true! If the machines are broken or the people are too tired, even the coolest idea won't work. We have to pick a project that can actually get its work done!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely. It would be a tragedy to fund a masterpiece of a proposal only to have it become a monument to unforeseen logistical failures. Pragmatism, in this instance, is the highest form of sophistication.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,Pragmatism is indeed necessary. We must avoid the trap of being dazzled by a proposal's ambition if the history of such projects shows they rarely reach their stated goals. Stability and utility are the only true metrics.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,"Let us remember that the heart of science is the people. A project is not a document, but a living breath of collaboration. We must choose the path where the human spirit is most supported.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Midori,,"I completely agree. When we look at the candidates, I hope we can find a project that balances ambitious goals with a realistic plan that doesn't overwhelm the researchers or their budget.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"I'm with you! I really hope we find a project that doesn't need too much from those struggling shared services, or one that has a plan to help out. Let's find a winner!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,A sentiment I share. It would be most prudent to favor a candidate whose methodology is resilient to the whims of nature and the fragility of infrastructure. Let us hope the candidates reflect such foresight.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,The evidence is clear. We should be wary of those who promise a revolution but lack a foundation. I will be looking for the candidate whose work offers lasting value rather than fleeting excitement.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Servas,,"As we prepare to meet the candidates, let us keep our hearts open and our minds clear. May we find a project that honors both the vision of the future and the reality of the present.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Midori,,I look forward to seeing the candidates. I hope we can all find a common ground that ensures the chosen project is both sustainable and supportive for everyone involved.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm ready! Let's look at the candidates and pick the one that's most likely to succeed without breaking anything or stressing everyone out. I can't wait to see who they are!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I shall join you in that anticipation. Let us hope the candidates possess not only intellectual brilliance but also the practical wisdom to navigate the chaos of the real world. I am ready.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"I am ready as well. Let us see which of these candidates offers a tangible contribution that will endure, rather than a promise that will eventually fade.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
